# Guild.ai Context Rule

Before planning, building, testing, or prioritizing any Guild.ai agent or Guild-related workflow, read `guild_context.md` from the workspace root.

Use that document as the source of truth for:

- The strategic goal of the Guild.ai engagement.
- Stakeholder context and communication style.
- Agent backlog tiers and sequencing.
- Multi-agent handoff requirements.
- Token-cost and harness constraints.
- Pricing and long-term positioning.

When producing Guild agent plans:

- Identify the agent tier.
- Prefer connected workflows over isolated one-off agents.
- Design outputs as structured inputs for another agent when possible.
- Flag plans that need indexing, semantic search, credential handling, or MCP infrastructure as platform/harness work.
- Keep 1-2 week agent builds separate from larger infrastructure initiatives.
